+# Specialty Narrowing Is an Uncached, Case-Insensitive Database Query
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+`REQ-VET-003` narrows the veterinarian directory to the veterinarians holding one named specialty, on the page and on the machine-readable list. The name matches whole, disregarding letter case. The vet repository caches its reads in one cache with no size limit and no eviction. The caller supplies the specialty name, so any cache keyed on it grows with whatever callers send. The three vendor schemas compare text differently: PostgreSQL is case-sensitive where H2 and MySQL are not. NG-9's narrowing admits further filters by shown attributes, so this choice sets the pattern for them.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Filter in memory over the cached whole directory.** Reuses the cache, but moves paging into the controller and places a matching rule outside the repository.
+2. **Derived query, cached in the vet cache.** Keeps the filter in the database, but keys an unbounded cache on caller-supplied text.
+3. **Derived query, uncached** (chosen). The database filters and pages; the cache holds only the unnarrowed reads.
+
+## Decision
+
+Narrowing by specialty is a Spring Data derived query on `VetRepository`. It compares the whole name case-insensitively inside the query and returns each veterinarian once. The narrowed reads carry no cache annotation. A request-derived value reaches the page's links only as a link-expression parameter, never through template preprocessing.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The cache stays keyed on values the application controls; a caller cannot grow it.
+- Case-insensitive matching behaves the same on all three vendors, unlike owner search on PostgreSQL.
+- Every narrowed request reaches the database. The directory is small, so the cost is accepted until a size figure says otherwise.
+- A later filter by another shown attribute follows the same shape.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Requirements:** REQ-VET-003
+
+## References
+
+- [Contracts](../system-design.md#contracts)
+- [Scale and Load](../system-design.md#scale-and-load)
+- [Non-goal ADR narrowing NG-9](2026-10-25-non-goal-narrow-veterinarian-search.md)
